A||N||3||Matt85_GT||Need help V6 only||||5||
Z||000000||Matt85_GT||04-08-2000||06:26 PM||||Would someone who has a good running V6 fiero please perform the following test?  Disconnect the injector six way connector it is located just below the MAP sensor thermostat side of the engine.  The connector has the letters A through F labeled on it.  Check the resistance with and ohmeter of the injector harness between <BR>B & A, B & D, C & A, and C & D.  Please tell me if you get resistance between all of these terminals and how much. Please respond<BR>Thanks, Matt 85 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||04-08-2000||07:37 PM||||86GT measures 3.7 Ohms and 3.8 Ohms across the injector banks.  A-B, C-D.  All others are infinity (many Megohms), as they should be.  I did not check E-F as it goes to a sensor I have not identified yet, and has no bearing on the injector resistance.  Hope this helps...D||||reg||1
Z||000002||Matt85_GT||04-08-2000||08:25 PM||||Thanks, could you also check if there is a complete circuit through those terminals.  I know there is on A and B, C and D, but not sure about the other two.||||reg||1
Z||000003||daved||04-09-2000||11:14 AM||||Matt, I learned something here...E-F measures 3.6 Ohms and is the Cold Start Injector!<BR>Dont see why GM stuck at that end of the engine...most engines have the cold start injectors near the throttle body.  It works well, so they must be on to something.  Good luck with your trouble-shooting.  D. ||||reg||1
